  "title": "THE PROMISE CAN CHANGE SHAPE",
  "period": "January",
  "passages": [
    "Some days I missed the goal. Some days I needed rest. Household chores and storm cleanup still happened. The ordinary logistics of life kept interrupting the transformation montage.",
    "I began learning how to adjust without treating every adjustment as defeat. A smaller practice could still count. Guidance from a friend could help. Mobility mattered. Preparation mattered. The handstand was becoming a lesson in how to continue a life, including the days that never looked impressive on camera."
  ],
  "reflections": [
    {
      "kind": "Notice",
      "prompt": "What would continuing look like on a hard day?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "Write",
      "prompt": "Write a smaller version of a promise you have made to yourself. What would still count on a difficult day?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "Try",
      "prompt": "Try the smaller promise once. Notice whether it leaves you more willing to return."
    }
  ],
